@baseUrl = http://localhost:5181
@authLimit = 5
@loginPassword = <set-a-local-test-password>
@loginEmail = <use-a-disposable-fixture-email>
@validToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@adminToken = <capture-locally-do-not-commit>
@largePayload = <generate-a-2-MB-json-body-locally>
@password200Characters = <generate-exactly-200-characters-locally>

# Safety and setup:
# - These tests are documentation/HTTP-client requests, not an authorization to mutate
#   NEBRASDB_Step1. Use only an isolated disposable database and disposable fixtures.
# - Set RateLimit:AuthPerMinute to 5 in a local test configuration/environment before
#   running the rate-limit block; do not change tracked appsettings.json.
# - The application currently has a Development HTTP URL at http://localhost:5181
#   and HTTPS at https://localhost:7265. Prefer HTTPS when its local certificate is
#   trusted. If it is untrusted, use the HTTP development URL for local testing only;
#   do not disable or weaken application security.
# - Never print credentials, tokens, hashes, or response bodies containing personal data.

### Required security headers — EXPECTED: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/lands

# Expected headers:
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
# X-Frame-Options: DENY
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
# Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

### Valid token through Authorization header — EXPECTED: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{validToken}}

### Token through query string — EXPECTED: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me?access_token=<valid-token>

### Tampered JWT — EXPECTED: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <tampered-token>

### Unsigned alg:none JWT — EXPECTED: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <unsigned-token>

### Deactivated token — EXPECTED: 401
# Requires a disposable fixture whose old token was captured before soft deletion.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <deactivated-user-old-token>

### Role-changed token — EXPECTED: 401
# Requires a disposable fixture whose database role was changed after token issuance.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer <role-changed-user-old-token>

